A||N||6||Monkeyman||Speaker probs on an IBM Thinkpad i series||||5||
Z||000000||Monkeyman||08-30-2001||06:30 AM||||I have an IBM Thinkpad "i" series laptop that runs well for the most part, but has developed an annoying speaker problem lately.  It seems that I get terrible feedback when I turn the volume up past about "3".  This happens during audio CD playback as well as any other software audio (you know what I mean).  I don't seem to have any other problems with the laptop (other than the fact that it's slow--gotta upgrade the RAM soon).  The audio/CD/etc player is "AudioRack64".  It's never given me any problems, either.  Any suggestions as to where my problem might be or what I can do to fix it?  I doubt that the speakers are blown as this problem came on quite suddenly and not during any audio use.  (Worked fine one time, then got the feedback/squeal the next time I used her.)<P>Any help would be greatly appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||5
Z||000001||84Bill||08-30-2001||09:11 AM||||Audio drivers are a PITA for that model but it sounds like there may be a hardware ( interupt ) problem there. The best sugguestion I have is go to the IBM site and get the drivers. Uninstall the old ones and replace with the now also update direct X This may help if not then nothing short of reinstalling the OS will help||||reg||1
Z||000002||Raydar||08-30-2001||09:53 AM||||Does it have a built-in mic? If so, maybe it's feeding back. You might try going in to your sound app. (Not familiar with Audio Rack) and muting the mic. If it's like the others apps I've seen, there should be a box to check or uncheck. If that doesn't work, see if there's an option to make your sound card HDX (half duplex) instead of FDX (full duplex).<BR>Purely a shot in the dark.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000003||84Bill||08-30-2001||01:40 PM||||Heh you know Raydar is prolly right  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>You mic is most likely on.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||08-30-2001||02:11 PM||||Thanx, guys.  I'll try that as soon as I figure out why my laptop won't come on.  (It worked yesterday or maybe the day before.)  Strange.  I push the "On" button and nothing happens.  If I had more money, I'd just buy another laptop and throw this one out.  I'm not in the mood for frustration today.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000005||Monkeyman||08-30-2001||02:25 PM||||I finally got the computer to come on.  I've had problems with the battery ever since I bought it.  (I bought it used late last year.)  It's never kept a charge.  Apparently, the computer won't work with a dead battery even if it's plugged in.  I removed the battery and the computer came on just fine.<P>Anyhow...back to the original problem.  I must need more sleep.  I muted the mike and...voila!  No more feedback.  Thanx a ton, guys.  That's the logical answer.  I don't know why I didn't think of it.  Either idiocy or the fact that I'm lucky to get 3 or 4 hours of sleep a night.  Once again, thanx millions.<P>------------------<BR>'Consciousness:  That annoying time between naps.'<P>MM||||reg||1
